A MODIFIED VERSION
------------------

This is a modified build of the Pangolin Windows client by Fossorial, Inc.
(https://github.com/fosrl/windows), Copyright (c) 2025 Fossorial, Inc.

Upstream states that files without a license header are licensed under AGPL-3,
and dual-licensing under the Fossorial Commercial License requires a separate
written agreement. No file in the upstream tree carries a commercial-license
header, so the whole of it is AGPL-3, and so is this derivative.

Modifications by ZTARC, beginning 23 August 2026:

  * Renamed and rebranded throughout — application name, Windows service name,
    configuration directory, tunnel adapter, named pipes, log file, icons and
    word marks.
  * Default server set to the ZTARC console; the upstream vendor's hosted
    service is no longer offered.
  * Removed links to pages that do not exist for this product (terms of service,
    privacy policy) and the menu entry that downloads the upstream vendor's CLI.
  * Added a version scheme that records which upstream release a build is based
    on, and a build counter of our own.
  * Icons are now looked for beside the executable before the installation
    directory.
  * Automatic update checks default to off.

None of these edits are made to the upstream tree itself. `upstream/` is a
pristine git submodule pinned to a released tag; every change above is expressed
as a rule under `brand/` and applied to a staged copy at build time. Reading
`brand/` alongside the submodule pin therefore shows exactly what was changed
and nothing else.


CORRESPONDING SOURCE
--------------------

The complete corresponding source for any binary we distribute is this
repository at the commit the binary was built from, together with the upstream
submodule at its recorded commit:

    https://github.com/ztarc/ztarc-windows

The client links to it from Preferences → About → Legal → "Source code (AGPL-3)".


